    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Implement a constant rate Token Bucket. It uses signed numbers and can go negative (if there is at least 1 token available to the borrower)</para>
<para>The expected workflow is to:<orderedlist>
<listitem><para>Define the limit with setRate()</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>For each possible event: a. Call <ref refid="classTokenRateLimiter_1ad7b2ab794fc2bdf66aa5d43db25fcf1f" kindref="member">AddTime()</ref> based on the time since last use. b. Call <ref refid="classTokenRateLimiter_1aac49f21eb5cc16bd38b2e1025269403b" kindref="member">GetRemainingTokens()</ref> to see if the wanted use is possible. c. If possible, call <ref refid="classTokenRateLimiter_1aa00dc2f8062840585865e62395bc8570" kindref="member">TakeTokens()</ref> to reduce the bucket. </para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
